  "corrections_2026_08_04": {
    "provenance": "Adversarial review of exp6093, each correction re-verified independently before being applied. Prior values are PRESERVED beside the corrected ones per the never-prune rule.",
    "corrections": [
      {
        "id": "C1_search_cost_is_a_constant",
        "severity": "blocking_false_field",
        "retracted": "dev_twin_arc_loop_solve.per_game[].treatment_search_cost == 6000 as a measurement, and the raw cells' search_cost_unit == 'max_expansions_exhausted' on 15 cells.",
        "why_wrong": "scripts/experiments/outer_loop_arc_devtwin_adapterfree_cell_20260803.py:166 and :176 write `search_cost: args.max_expansions` in BOTH treatment branches and never pass `stats=` to graph_explore_solve_v2. The value is the BUDGET. All the code knew was `traj is None`; it could not observe exhaustion. The control arm's `states_expanded` was always real, so the per-game table printed a measurement and a constant side by side as if comparable.",
        "replaced_with": "results/experiment_6094_arc_devtwin_true_search_cost.json -- all 25 treatment cells re-run with stats={}.",
        "measured": {
          "of_15_failing_cells_labelled_exhausted_truly_exhausted": 13,
          "sc25_true_expansions_at_6000_and_at_30000": 24,
          "sc25_distinct_states": 1,
          "g50t_true_expansions_at_6000_and_at_30000": 4100,
          "g50t_distinct_states": 843,
          "cn04_and_dc22_re_probed_at_30000_truly_exhausted": true
        },
        "headline_impact": "none -- 24/25 -> 10/25, the sign test and 14/25 at 5x budget are unaffected."
      },
      {
        "id": "C2_capability_wall_wrong_for_two_games",
        "severity": "interpretive_retraction",
        "retracted": "dev_twin_long_budget_probe's 'capability wall, not a budget wall' reading as applied to all 11 still-failing games.",
        "replaced_with": "9 of 11 genuinely exhausted 6000 and again 30000 expansions -- capability wall, reading stands. sc25 and g50t terminated with budget UNUSED at both budgets, so the 5x probe was VACUOUS for them; their failure is a FRONTIER COLLAPSE under the generic state abstraction, not a search-depth limit. sc25 is extreme: 1 distinct state discovered. exp6093's prose already reached this for sc25 ('frontier exhausted', wall_s 4.92) while publishing the contradictory number, and never applied it to g50t.",
        "guard_this_violated": "The run's own honesty guard #1 (explored_out audit -- distinguish a frontier collapse from a saving) was applied to the scored path, where 0 cells explored out, and never to the dev twin, which is where the collapse actually happened."
      },
      {
        "id": "C3_dev_twin_sign_test_is_post_hoc_not_pre_registered",
